---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const open = `const opened = await connection.records.open("Notes/today.md", {
  autosave: { idleMs: 1_000 },
  timeoutMs: 8_000
});
if (!opened.ok) return renderProblem(opened.problem);
const { session, release } = opened.value;

const unsubscribe = session.subscribe(() => render(session.getSnapshot()));
editor.onChange((text) => session.setBody(text));
properties.onChange((patch) => session.patchFrontmatter(patch));`;

const follow = `const watch = await connection.watch({}, { timeoutMs: 20_000 });
if (watch.ok) {
  const stopFollowing = connection.records.follow(watch.value);
  // On sign-out: stopFollowing(); watch.value.close();
}`;

const leave = `const flushed = await session.flush({ timeoutMs: 8_000 });
if (!flushed.ok) {
  if (flushed.problem.code === "concurrent_modification") {
    showConflict(session.getSnapshot()); // local body and snapshot.remote
  } else {
    renderProblem(flushed.problem);
  }
}
unsubscribe();
release();`;

const resolve = `session.resolve({ keep: "mine" });   // write local changes over the newer record
session.resolve({ keep: "theirs" }); // take the newer record
session.resolve({ body: merged });   // save text the user merged`;

const react = `const store = externalStore(session);

function useRecord() {
  return useSyncExternalStore(store.subscribe, store.getSnapshot, store.getSnapshot);
}`;

const adapter = `import { MdbaseRecordSession } from "@mdbase-dev/connect";
import type { MdbaseRecordSessionAdapter } from "@mdbase-dev/connect/advanced";

const adapter: MdbaseRecordSessionAdapter<Note> = {
  revision: (note) => note.revision,
  body: (note) => note.body,
  frontmatter: (note) => note.frontmatter,
  write: (base, change, options) => notes.write(base, change, options), // ConnectOutcome<Note>
  read: (base, options) => notes.read(base.id, options),
  recover: (requestId, options) => notes.recover(requestId, options),
  isPending: (requestId) => notes.isPending(requestId)
};
const session = new MdbaseRecordSession(note, adapter, { autosave: { idleMs: 650 } });`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Editing records"
  description="Keep one record open while people type: autosave, conflicts, lost responses, renames and deletions handled by one shared session."
  active="operations"
  headings={[
    { href: "#open", label: "Open a record" },
    { href: "#follow", label: "Stay current" },
    { href: "#states", label: "States" },
    { href: "#conflicts", label: "Conflicts" },
    { href: "#leave", label: "Leave safely" },
    { href: "#react", label: "React" },
    { href: "#custom", label: "Custom storage" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    An application that lets people type into a record should not call{" "}
    <code>update()</code> on every change. Open the record as a session
    instead. The session saves after a pause in typing, never runs two writes
    for the same record, and tells your interface what state the record is in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="open">Open a record</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={open} language="ts" label="editor.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>open()</code> reads the record and returns a lease: the session and a{" "}
    <code>release()</code> function for this view. Every view that opens the
    same path shares one session, so an application never has two competing
    writers for a record. Each save sends only the body and the frontmatter
    keys that changed, checked against the revision they were based on.
  </p>

  <h2 id="follow">Stay current while it is open</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={follow} language="ts" label="watch.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>follow()</code> routes collection changes to open sessions. A record
    changed elsewhere is re-read, a renamed record keeps its session at the new
    path, and a deleted record keeps its local text. After a change gap every
    open record is re-read. The session recognizes its own saves, including
    when the saved text comes back normalized before the save has finished,
    so they are never mistaken for someone else's edit.
  </p>

  <h2 id="states">States</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>saved</code>: the text is the saved record.</li>
    <li><code>unsaved</code>: local changes wait for autosave or <code>flush()</code>.</li>
    <li><code>saving</code>: a write is in flight. Typing continues; newer text is saved next.</li>
    <li><code>conflict</code>: the record changed elsewhere in a part edited locally.</li>
    <li><code>recovery</code>: a save's response was lost. The same save is recovered exactly; nothing new is written until it is. This includes a save interrupted by a reload: <code>open()</code> resumes it.</li>
    <li><code>error</code>: the last save failed. Local text is kept, and nothing retries in the background.</li>
    <li><code>deleted</code>: the record no longer exists. Local text is kept.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <code>snapshot.problem</code> holds the typed problem behind{" "}
    <code>error</code> and <code>recovery</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="conflicts">Resolve conflicts</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={resolve} language="ts" label="conflict.ts" />
  <p>
    A change made elsewhere is a conflict only when it touched something edited
    locally: the body, or a frontmatter key the user changed. Otherwise the
    session builds on the newer record without asking. If the other change
    produced exactly the local text, the record is simply saved.
  </p>

  <h2 id="leave">Leave safely</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={leave} language="ts" label="leave.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>flush()</code> saves until nothing is left, or returns why it cannot.
    Releasing the last view never cancels a save in progress; the session is
    dropped once it has nothing left to save.
  </p>

  <h2 id="react">Use it from React</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={react} language="tsx" label="use-record.tsx" />

  <h2 id="custom">Records behind your own storage</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={adapter} language="ts" label="custom-session.ts" />
  <p>
    Applications that reach records through their own repository or a test
    double construct the session with an adapter from{" "}
    <code>@mdbase-dev/connect/advanced</code>. Adapters report failures as{" "}
    <code>ConnectOutcome</code> values. A <code>file_not_found</code> problem
    from <code>read</code> marks the record deleted, and <code>recover</code>{" "}
    must continue the original write through its pending mutation, never send
    a new one.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
